{# Widget "browse" — THE HUB ITSELF (FL·01).

   STATIC TWIN of files.widgets.js's `browse` entry. Rendered by BOTH the hub and
   the widget library.

   One filter row, one search, one shape toggle and ONE result set — the grid and
   the list are the same page of the same files in two shapes, never two
   queries — and the Shell's register foot under both. Every chip is a query
   parameter and nothing more:
     → GET /files?module=&area=&kind=&day=&backend=&thumb=&q=&view=&page=&per=

   THE ROW ITSELF IS `_filters.html.twig`, shared with every other widget that
   draws filters, so this surface cannot grow two filter bars that disagree.

   WHICH SHAPE IS SHOWING IS THE SERVER'S ANSWER TOO. It rides in the same query
   as the chips, so a narrowed hub stays in the shape it was read in and a list
   survives pressing a chip.

   There is NO upload control here, and there is none anywhere else on this
   surface either. A file arrives by being attached to a record, on that record's
   own page. #}
{% import '@UhifadhiStorage/files/_ui.html.twig' as ui %}
<div class="c" data-w="browse">
    <span class="tab">Every file, across every module<span class="src">&middot; a picture is a thumbnail, never the original</span></span>
    {{ include('@UhifadhiStorage/files/_filters.html.twig') }}
    <div data-f-shapewrap{{ files is empty ? ' hidden' : '' }}>
        <div class="f-grid" data-f-grid{{ filter.view == 'grid' ? '' : ' hidden' }}>{%- for file in rows -%}{{ ui.tile(file) }}{%- endfor -%}</div>
        <div data-f-listwrap{{ filter.view == 'list' ? '' : ' hidden' }}><table class="f-list" data-f-list>{{ ui.listhead() }}<tbody>{%- for file in rows -%}{{ ui.row(file, places) }}{%- endfor -%}</tbody></table></div>
    </div>
    {{ include('@Shell/_foot.html.twig', {
        count: table.total, noun: 'files', one: 'file',
        perPage: table.size, page: table.page, pages: table.pages, links: links,
        hidden: files is empty,
    }, with_context: false) }}
    {{ ui.empty(files is empty) }}
    {# A way of looking across every module's files at once, not a shelf you put
       things on — which is also why there is no upload button: a file arrives by
       being attached to a record, on that record's own page. #}
    <div class="use"><b>Every tile says who owns it.</b> Files hang off records &middot; no upload here &mdash; a file arrives on its record&rsquo;s own page.</div>
</div>
